  "content": {
    "title": "Daredevil: Born Again Season 2 premieres Tuesday on Disney+",
    "text": "Charlie Cox as Daredevil in a scene from “Daredevil: Born Again.” (Disney+/Marvel Television) by: Jesse Gill Posted: Mar 21, 2026 / 02:54 PM PDT Updated: Mar 21, 2026 / 04:01 PM PDT Marvel’s most popular Disney+ series is back. Daredevil: Born Again Season 2 premieres Tuesday, March 24 on Disney+, and it’s shaping up to be the biggest chapter yet for Matt Murdock and the Hell’s Kitchen corner of the MCU. Season 2 picks up with Wilson Fisk – now Mayor of New York City – hunting down Daredevil as public enemy number one. Beneath the mask, Matt Murdock fights back from the shadows to dismantle Fisk’s corrupt empire. The season spans eight episodes, releasing weekly after Tuesday’s premiere. The biggest draw for longtime fans is the return of Krysten Ritter as Jessica Jones – her first appearance in the MCU since her Netflix series was canceled in 2018. Charlie Cox and Vincent D’Onofrio are back as Daredevil and Kingpin, along with returning fan favorites Deborah Ann Woll as Karen Page and Wilson Bethel as Bullseye. New to the cast is Matthew Lillard, whose mysterious role has been kept tightly under wraps. If that weren’t enough to get excited about, Marvel announced that Season 3 is already in production, with filming underway in New York. Cox himself confirmed it on Jimmy Kimmel Live!, joking that he flew straight to the show from a late-night action shoot covered in fake blood and scars. Season 3 is expected to premiere in March 2027. Looking further ahead, fans of the original Netflix Defenders lineup have even more to look forward to: Finn Jones is set to return as Iron Fist and Elodie Yung as Elektra in Season 3, fueling speculation about a full Defenders reunion down the line. Daredevil: Born Again Season 2 premieres Tuesday, March 24 at 6 p.m. PT / 9 p.m. ET on Disney+.",
